1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:03,440
Regarding Cheung Siu-chung's death inside
a village house in Wan Mei Village,

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:05,840
we don't know if someone forced
a sugarcane inside his mouth.

3
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:07,360
We won't rule out homicide.

4
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:10,160
We need you down at the Police station
to facilitate our investigation.

5
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,920
Cheung Tai-di's parentage is rather unusual.

6
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:14,560
Maybe because she's not my child.

7
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:17,920
Miss Tai-di never liked Master Chung.

8
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,120
She wanted him dead.

9
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,520
I did hate her.

10
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,480
Chung...

11
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:31,040
Hello, 999?

12
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:33,600
Yes, someone is unconscious in
Wan Mei Village.

13
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:37,120
Does anyone else live here?

14
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:38,720
No.

15
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:52,760
Control, send a coffin van to
No. 38 Wan Mei Village.

16
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:06,480
Chung...don't scare me...Chung!

17
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:08,640
The paramedics suspect when Cheung Siu-chung
was eating sugarcane,

18
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:10,480
scraps went inside his trachea by mistake

19
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,520
and caused him to suffocate.

20
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:13,600
Initially, it will be treated as a case
of a dead body found.

21
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:15,920
My brother has had epilepsy
since he was little.

22
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,920
But he was taking meds for it.

23
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,000
He hasn't had an episode in a long time.

24
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:22,240
How did you come across the victim?

25
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,640
It was his birthday; I bought him a cake.

26
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,320
When I walked in,

27
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:30,800
I found him lying on the floor
with a sugarcane is his mouth.

28
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:33,840
I didn't buy him any sugarcane.

29
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:35,360
I don't know where it came from.

30
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:37,280
Was the village house his home?

31
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:42,640
He was having problems at home

32
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:44,080
and didn't want to stay there.

33
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:47,200
I asked a friend to let him stay there.

34
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:51,120
You arranged for Chung to stay out?

35
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:53,280
We were all looking for him,

36
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:54,640
why didn't you say something?

37
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:57,280
You knew he had limited intelligence.

38
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:59,360
How could you let him live on his own?

39
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:00,880
What was your intention?

40
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:03,560
If you didn't help Chung,

41
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:06,080
he wouldn't stay out for so long

42
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:09,200
and choked on a sugarcane and
triggered his epilepsy.

43
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,000
If it happened at home,

44
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:12,720
we could have saved him.

45
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:15,040
He didn't have to die.

46
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:17,400
I'm sorry...

47
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:20,480
What's the use of apologizing now?

48
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:23,160
Chung is dead.

49
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,440
And you!

50
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:30,400
Chung is Father's son after all.

51
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:32,080
Why can't you accept him?

52
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:33,920
You made him run away from home.

53
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,920
You had a part in killing him.

54
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:38,120
Enough of your yelling.

55
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:40,480
Did you even care about Chung?

56
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,120
Of course I care about him.

57
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:43,440
I looked everywhere for him.

58
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:45,600
You're not worried about losing him.

59
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:48,080
You're worried about the inheritance.

60
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:52,120
Chung ran away because he was ashamed of you

61
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:54,880
who messed with your father-in-law.

62
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,840
You made a cuckold out of Chi.

63
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:00,160
And my grandson became an
illegitimate child.

64
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:03,560
Enough! Stop arguing!

65
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:06,400
It was your non-stop bickering

66
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,880
that drove Chung out of this house.

67
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,360
Where is it?

68
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:17,440
Chung's watch is gone!

69
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:19,760
You mean the watch Chung was wearing?

70
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,200
Where is it?

71
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:25,360
When the paramedics were trying to
revive Chung,

72
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:27,280
the watchband broke
and it fell to the ground

73
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:29,600
I picked it up and put it in my pocket.

74
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:31,280
But now it's gone.

75
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:35,280
I gave him that watch on his 18th birthday.

76
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:37,040
It was of great sentimental value.

77
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:39,200
You must find it.

78
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,400
Looks like it's gone...

79
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:49,360
Chung is dead. Even the watch is gone...

80
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:55,840
What's with the racket?

81
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:00,960
Chi...

82
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,520
Wait!

83
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:09,440
Chung is my son. I'll tell him.

84
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:19,760
Are we disturbing you?

85
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,640
Let's go upstairs...

86
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:46,960
Snail, Chung B can't play with us anymore.

87
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:49,440
Hurry up...don't look back!

88
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:51,840
Hurry! Mine is faster than yours...

89
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:53,840
Hurry!
Yours is too slow...

90
00:05:54,360 --> 00:06:03,760
Like Grandpa, he's a star in the sky.

91
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:07,840
Get up! The school bus is leaving...

92
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,640
Happy birthday...Mom!

93
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:13,120
It's so pretty...

94
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:14,480
It took me a long time to draw...

95
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:16,480
That's very sweet of you...

96
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:25,440
We'll never...see Chung B again.

97
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:31,600
Papa missed you...

98
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:40,160
Chi, stop crying! Don't be so sad.

99
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:43,360
He's not even your son.

100
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:49,040
The body found in Wan Mei Village

101
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,120
may be classified as murder.

102
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,400
It's assigned to us.

103
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,520
The victim was Cheung Siu-chung.

104
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:57,760
In the autopsy report, the medical examiner
estimated his time of death

105
00:06:57,880 --> 00:07:02,160
to be between 11p.m. on the 15th and
1a.m. on the 16th of this month.

106
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:04,960
We don't know if the sugarcane was
forced inside his mouth.

107
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:08,000
The clothing fiber found on the sugarcane

108
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:10,480
did not match the victim's.

109
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:12,160
It may belong to someone else.

110
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,200
We won't rule out homicide.

111
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:18,520
Folks from I.T. unlocked his phone.

112
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:21,200
According to the phone log and
text messages,

113
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:25,920
Cheung Siu-chung only contacted
his sister Cheung Tai-di

114
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:28,080
and a lawyer called Mok Kai-wing
in the last few days.

115
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,440
Let me introduce myself,

116
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:30,640
I'm Mok Kai-wing, a lawyer.

117
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,480
Mr. Cheung Siu-chung authorized me

118
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:35,200
to set up a trust fund to manage his assets.

119
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:37,200
I would like to read out the contents.

120
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:40,200
Mr. Cheung Siu-chung wished to leave

121
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:44,400
a 3-storey duplex in Ko Cho Village
to Ms. Leung Yuet-ping

122
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:46,200
with a proviso that

123
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:50,160
Ms. Tang Suk-han and Mr. Cheung Wang-chi
have both passed away

124
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:53,200
before Ms. Leung Yuet-ping can sell
or rent out the duplex.

125
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:55,920
The remaining $70M assets,

126
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,160
will be used to maintain a balanced
investment portfolio,

127
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:00,520
the profits of which will take care
of members of the Cheung family

128
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:02,960
and given to each member
in a monthly allowance

129
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:05,040
in the following amount
in Hong Kong dollars.

130
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,640
Ms. Tang Suk-han $50K,

131
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:08,240
Ms. Leung Yuet-ping $50K,

132
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,920
and Mr. Cheung Wang Chi $30K

133
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,040
until they pass away.

134
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:13,760
Mr. Cheung Siu-chung already signed on it.

135
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:14,640
Hold on!

136
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:17,440
Chung doesn't know anything
about wealth management.

137
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:19,920
How did he know about trust funds?

138
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:21,840
Did someone teach him?

139
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,600
How did he know to contact you?

140
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:25,760
Mr. Cheung contacted me personally.

141
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:28,360
As to why he wanted to set up a trust fund,

142
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:29,520
I don't exactly know.

143
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:32,080
Why don't I finish reading the document?

144
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:34,240
Kin-kwok left us this house.

145
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:36,680
Why would Chung give it to that woman?

146
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:39,440
As Mr. Cheung Siu-chung's counsel,

147
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:42,800
I'm only carrying out my client's wishes.

148
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:44,320
It doesn't make sense.

149
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:45,920
I'd like to point out one thing.

150
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:49,800
Whether Mr. Cheung Siu-chung's time of death
was before or after midnight,

151
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:52,160
is crucial to the asset allocation.

152
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:56,320
If he died on or after midnight
on October 16,

153
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,600
he would have been 21 years old

154
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:00,720
and was entitled to inherit
Mr. Cheung Kin-kwok's estate.

155
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:05,360
The assets will be allocated according to
the trust fund set up by him.

156
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,880
What if it was before midnight?

157
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:10,640
If the time of death was before
midnight on October 15,

158
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:12,080
he was not yet 21 years old.

159
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:15,200
Then he was not entitled to inherit
Mr. Cheung Kin-kwok's estate.

160
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:17,840
According to the Intestates'
Estates Ordinance,

161
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:20,320
50% will go to the spouse

162
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,120
and the remaining 50% will be equally
distributed among his children.

163
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:26,400
The actual time of death is still pending
the autopsy report.

164
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:28,000
I also wish to point out,

165
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:31,120
prior to Mr. Cheung Siu-chung's accident,
he contacted me

166
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:34,000
and indicated he wished to amend the
provisions of the trust fund.

167
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:38,080
My office has sent out the revised document

168
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:41,760
but unfortunately, before we received
any response from him,

169
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:42,880
Mr. Cheung passed away.

170
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:46,880
Madam Han, the Police is here.

171
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:50,000
I'm Senior Police Constable Sze King
of the Crime Unit in New Territories East.

172
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:51,280
Police Constable Cheung Yau-ming.

173
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:52,480
What is it?

174
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:55,760
Regarding Cheung Siu-chung's death inside
a village house in Wan Mei Village,

175
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:58,160
the medical examiner finished
the autopsy report.

176
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:00,080
We won't rule out homicide.

177
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:03,200
We need you down at the Police station
to facilitate our investigation.

178
00:10:15,040 --> 00:10:18,160
Ms. Law Suet-chau, on the night
Cheung Siu-chung died,

179
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:21,760
the night of October 15
and after midnight on October 16,

180
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:22,640
where were you?

181
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:28,320
That night...like always,
after we finished dinner,

182
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:30,080
we went back to our rooms.

183
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:32,960
I finished doing the dishes

184
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:34,560
and went to sleep in my room.

185
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:40,000
After 12 o'clock,
I heard about Master Chung.

186
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:43,800
Between the night of the 15th
and after midnight on the 16th,

187
00:10:43,920 --> 00:10:46,720
you and your husband Cheung Wang-chi
were home the whole time?

188
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:48,880
Chi goes to bed around 9 o'clock.

189
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:51,600
That's the time we usually turn in.

190
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:55,360
Your father-in-law left everything
to Cheung Siu-chung,

191
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:58,480
was your mother-in-law very upset?

192
00:10:58,680 --> 00:11:02,080
Yes, we have been arguing about this.

193
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:04,240
It was Father's wishes

194
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:06,080
but Mother couldn't accept it.

195
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:08,880
She thought I persuaded Father
to leave everything to Chung.

196
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,480
She took out her frustration on Chung

197
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:11,760
and made him run away from home.

198
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,560
Was there any other reasons?

199
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:17,440
I couldn't think of any.

200
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:19,800
Cheung Siu-chung went missing for so long,

201
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:21,040
you were not worried at all?

202
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:24,720
Of course I was. But I couldn't find him.

203
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:26,080
Besides, he told me he was safe.

204
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:27,440
What did he tell you?

205
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:28,320
(2 days after Chung left)

206
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:30,080
He left a voice message

207
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:32,000
and said he needed time to think.

208
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,600
So I decided to give him space.

209
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:36,000
The night Cheung Siu-chung died,
where were you?

210
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:40,640
I was in bed by 10 o'clock.

211
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,600
Your husband left everything
to your grandson.

212
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:44,640
How do you feel about that?

213
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:46,720
I felt it was unfair for my son.

214
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:49,600
You were angry with Cheung Siu-chung
over the money?

215
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:54,400
Not exactly! It was Tai-di's fault.

216
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:56,960
She never cared about what went on at home.

217
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,880
But she seemed awfully helpful

218
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,400
and found Chung a place to stay.

219
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:02,880
I bet she wanted to coax her brother

220
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,800
into splitting the money with her.

221
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:08,960
Cheung Tai-di, do you know why
Cheung Siu-chung ran away from home?

222
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:11,040
Money.

223
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:14,080
Grandpa left him everything.

224
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:15,760
Grandma and Mom didn't get anything.

225
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:18,320
Chung was caught in between.

226
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:20,880
When did you arrive at the village house
in Wan Mei Village

227
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,480
to find Cheung Siu-chung?

228
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,880
I went drinking with friends.

229
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:27,200
It was around midnight when I left.

230
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:28,560
I went straight to the village house.

231
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,840
But I wasn't sure of the exact time.

232
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:35,360
Everyone claimed they had an alibi.

233
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:36,800
But judging from the video,

234
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:39,520
they all seemed to be hiding something.

235
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,840
Especially Cheung Tai-di.

236
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:44,320
As a lawyer she's prudent

237
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:46,400
and chose her words carefully.

238
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:49,040
My instincts tell me something is not right.

239
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:51,440
She was the first person at the scene

240
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,400
and called it in.

241
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,760
She also hid her brother from the family.

242
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,160
Too bad the village house had no CCTV.

243
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:57,840
We didn't know who was there.

244
00:12:58,040 --> 00:12:59,680
What did Cheung Tai-di say

245
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:01,840
about Cheung Siu-chung
running away from home?

246
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:04,000
I was going home that day...

247
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:06,400
and saw Chung bolted out of the house
looking agitated.

248
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,560
I was worried about him

249
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:10,560
and followed him to the pier.

250
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:16,080
Chung, what is it?

251
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:21,360
Sis...I'm so unhappy.

252
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:25,280
I'm confused. I don't want to go home.

253
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:30,080
Why don't I find you a place to stay
for a few days?

254
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:31,600
So you can calm down, OK?

255
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:38,640
In other words, you told Cheung Siu-chung
to leave home?

256
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:40,080
You can say that.

257
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:42,000
According to Leung Yuet-ping,

258
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:45,520
Cheung Siu-chung had a smart watch
that recorded his heartbeat.

259
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:47,280
It went missing.

260
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:50,000
We asked the paramedics

261
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:51,920
and they said you picked it up.

262
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:55,040
Yes, but somehow it fell out.

263
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:58,880
Did you persuade Cheung Siu-chung
to set up the trust fund?

264
00:13:59,160 --> 00:14:01,440
I only wanted to help him solve the problem.

265
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:03,600
(The day Chung ran away from home)

266
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:06,320
Sis, Grandma is mad at me.

267
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:10,560
I felt bad Mom lied to her for so long.

268
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:13,040
I want to give her some money.

269
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:17,520
But if Mom found out, she'd be upset.

270
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:20,400
What do you think I should do?

271
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:23,200
You can set up a trust fund.

272
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:25,680
Leave the house to Mom,

273
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:30,080
but on the condition that only after
Grandma and Dad have passed away,

274
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,920
before she'll get sole ownership.

275
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:34,800
For the rest of the assets,

276
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:37,360
share them with Grandma, Mom and Dad

277
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:39,920
as a monthly allowance.

278
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:43,040
You must state everything clearly

279
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:45,440
so they won't have cause to argue again.

280
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:50,560
And we can still live together?

281
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:53,280
Yes! If anything should happen,

282
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,200
I can help you deal with it

283
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:56,160
And you won't have to worry.

284
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:00,880
I must give you something.

285
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:03,760
Definitely not! I have a job.

286
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:05,040
I can make money.

287
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,920
Don't let them know or they'll nag.

288
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:09,920
You'll have no peace.

289
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:13,200
You're so brilliant.

290
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:17,680
The lawyer Mok Kai-wing who set up
the trust fund is your friend?

291
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:21,200
Yes! Chung wanted me to handle it.

292
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,280
But I don't want to get involved.

293
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:24,400
There's a conflict of interests.

294
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:26,240
So I introduced him to a friend.

295
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:29,520
You were there when the trust fund
was drafted?

296
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:30,560
That's correct.

297
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:33,600
Your Grandfather didn't leave you anything?

298
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:35,200
You're OK with that?

299
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:37,760
Grandpa was known for his
male preference mentality.

300
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:39,040
It was like that for over 20 years.

301
00:15:39,280 --> 00:15:40,480
I'd be shocked if he left me anything.

302
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:44,000
Cheung Kin-kwok gave $100M to
Cheung Siu-chung.

303
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:47,600
Everyone, including Cheung Tai-di
didn't get a dime.

304
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:50,920
Would anyone be so broadminded?

305
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:54,400
There's something unusual about
Cheung Tai-di's parentage.

306
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:57,680
How was Cheung Tai-di's relationship
with Cheung Siu-chung?

307
00:15:58,360 --> 00:16:00,080
Chung was nice to everybody.

308
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:02,000
Tai-di is rather indifferent

309
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:03,200
and doesn't get involved.

310
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:05,520
Maybe because she's not my child.

311
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,480
Before I married into this family,

312
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:12,480
Chi had a sexual relationship with
a resident at the DAC,

313
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:15,440
Tai-di's mother is also mentally challenged.

314
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:18,240
I'm not sure if my mother-in-law
wanted to save face

315
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:20,160
or didn't want to look after another
mentally challenged person.

316
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:21,840
She refused to let that woman marry
into the family.

317
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:23,680
She only took in the baby.

318
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:26,080
Tai-di grew up without her mother.

319
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:29,040
Maybe that's why she has a chip
on her shoulder.

320
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:32,240
Chau raised Tai-di.

321
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:36,080
Maybe she doesn't think we care about her.

322
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:39,600
She's wears a scowl on her face
and ignores us.

323
00:16:39,840 --> 00:16:42,560
Because she grew up without her mother?

324
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,480
That's possible.

325
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:47,560
I know she hates me the most.

326
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:50,800
But I don't care. Let her hate me.

327
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:54,080
Grandma was the reason I couldn't see my
biological mother.

328
00:16:54,440 --> 00:16:56,600
I did hate her.

329
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:02,080
Tai-di, you're home.

330
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:04,840
Father and I had business in Kowloon.

331
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:08,720
Chung will go to the tutor after
he gets out of school.

332
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:10,240
Don't just focus on your own stuff.

333
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:11,640
Make sure you watch over him, OK?

334
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:12,480
I will.

335
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:13,320
Let's go.

336
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:23,040
Tai-di, have you seen Grandpa?

337
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:24,040
No.

338
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:26,400
What about your Mom?

339
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:27,920
I don't know.

340
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:31,200
According to the helper, Auntie Chau,

341
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:34,160
Cheung Tai-di had a scary dark side
even when she was little.

342
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:36,560
She could fool others, but not me.

343
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:40,120
She never liked Master Chung

344
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,280
and wanted him dead.

345
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:42,480
I hate you...

346
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:43,440
What are you doing?

347
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:50,880
Chung, don't worry! I'll save you!

348
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:54,120
What a klutz!

349
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:57,840
Miss Tai-di's kindness towards Master Chung
is just an act.

350
00:17:58,040 --> 00:18:01,200
Did you tell anyone about this?

351
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:04,880
No, I feel sorry for Miss Tai-di.

352
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:06,720
Besides, I raised her

353
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:08,280
and have feelings towards her.

354
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:11,120
I don't want her to get kicked out.

355
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:15,760
Leung Yuet-ping mentioned
Cheung Tai-di wanted to study abroad

356
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:17,040
and needed a lot of money.

357
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:18,800
Cheung Siu-chung wouldn't listen to her,

358
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,720
they argued and she killed him?

359
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:23,680
The medical examiner said
Cheung Siu-chung's time of death

360
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:28,600
should between 11p.m. on October 15 and
1a.m. on October 16.

361
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:33,520
Cheung Tai-di claimed between 10:30p.m.
and midnight on October 15,

362
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:35,120
she was drinking with friends at a bar.

363
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:38,160
We can ask her friends and
check the CCTV at the bar

364
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:39,600
and we'll know if she was lying.

365
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:42,280
Ask the fruit stands in Ko Cho Village

366
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:45,360
to see if the Cheungs or anyone else
bought any sugarcanes.

367
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:48,880
Or the sugarcane could be bought
from elsewhere.

368
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:50,400
Try to find out as much as we can.

369
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:51,320
Right!

370
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:54,040
Mom! Honey!

371
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:55,040
Good boy!

372
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:57,120
When you gave your statements,

373
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:59,280
did you shoot off your mouth
to the Police?

374
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:02,000
Don't wash your dirty laundry in public.

375
00:19:02,320 --> 00:19:04,880
Kin-kwok was well respected in the village.

376
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:09,560
If word got out, we'd be humiliated.

377
00:19:09,800 --> 00:19:12,240
I only answered what the Police asked me.

378
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:13,680
I didn't say anything about Master Kwok.

379
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:19,680
The instigator should keep her mouth shut.

380
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,680
This is nothing to be proud of.

381
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:24,360
You're the instigator.

382
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:25,680
I haven't said anything.

383
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:28,000
But you practically ignored Tai-di.

384
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:29,520
I'm not sure if she said anything.

385
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:31,920
Have some tea, Madam Han.

386
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:35,920
Judging from the officers' reaction,

387
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:38,120
I don't think they know anything.

388
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:40,600
The officer told me just now,

389
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:43,560
Chung almost drowned when he was little.

390
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:47,440
Tai-di tried to kill him out of jealousy.

391
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,640
What?

392
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:54,880
I also didn't expect Tai-di would
persuade Chung to give her $2M.

393
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,800
That's why I told the Police

394
00:19:57,880 --> 00:20:01,120
Tai-di wanted to study abroad
and needed a lot of money.

395
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:02,720
How did you know about that?

396
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:06,600
Chung asked me for his red packet money.

397
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:08,640
I asked him why he needed it.

398
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:11,880
He told me he wanted to give it to Tai-di
so she could study abroad.

399
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:15,760
See? She's still held up at the
Police station.

400
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,560
They must have found something suspicious.

401
00:20:23,240 --> 00:20:27,120
You're not pleased because
you were left out of the trust fund.

402
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:28,720
That's why you persuaded Cheung Siu-chung

403
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:31,680
to amend it, add a new clause

404
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:32,960
and give you $2M.

405
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:36,400
I only know about the original trust fund.

406
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:38,640
I didn't know there was a revision

407
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:40,960
or Chung wanted to give me $2M.

408
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:43,520
Yes, I'm friends with Mr. Mok,

409
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,640
but on account of confidentiality
between lawyers,

410
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:47,640
he didn't tell me anything.

411
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:51,040
The night he died,
Cheung Siu-chung texted you.

412
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:54,400
"Sis, I won't listen to you anymore."

413
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:56,880
"It's my money, I'll decide
what to do with it".

414
00:20:57,280 --> 00:20:58,480
You have read it.

415
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:02,400
(The night of the incident)

416
00:21:02,520 --> 00:21:03,680
I finished drinking with my friends

417
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:04,960
and I remembered it was Chung's birthday.

418
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:06,840
I bought a cake and went to
the village house.

419
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,960
But there was no answer.

420
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:11,680
So I took out my phone to call him.

421
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:13,360
That was when I saw the message.

422
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:15,360
Sis, I won't listen to you anymore.

423
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,520
It's my money, I'll decide
what to do with it.

424
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:19,640
He's so pig-headed.

425
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:21,520
That's only your version.

426
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:24,800
The truth is he decided not to
give you any money,

427
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:26,400
and texted you.

428
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:27,920
You were unresolved

429
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:31,560
and wanted to convince him under
the pretext of celebrating his birthday.

430
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:32,360
I only want $2M...

431
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:34,280
You couldn't reach an agreement
and started to argue...

432
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:36,320
Don't yell at me, Sis!
I'm not your sister.

433
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:37,360
We have different mothers.

434
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:40,520
I only want $2M...

435
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:42,080
Because Cheung Siu-chung refused
to listen to you,

436
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:44,640
you became unhinged and killed him
by mistake.

437
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:02,280
On the unpeeled part of the sugarcane,

438
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:05,040
we found fingerprints that
didn't belong to Cheung Siu-chung.

439
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:07,880
Fingerprint recognition confirmed
they belonged to you.

440
00:22:10,080 --> 00:22:10,800
Chung...

441
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,960
I removed the sugarcane in his mouth.

442
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:14,320
Of course it had my fingerprints on it.

443
00:22:14,440 --> 00:22:16,280
According to the text messages,

444
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:20,640
Cheung Siu-chung texted Mr. Mok
he received the revised document.

445
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:23,840
But we couldn't find it at the scene.

446
00:22:24,280 --> 00:22:26,000
Because he wouldn't listen to you,

447
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:29,360
you killed him in a fit of anger
and took the document with you.

448
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:33,360
This is merely your speculation.

449
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:35,200
You have no proof.

450
00:22:56,920 --> 00:22:58,360
Sis...
Chung?

451
00:22:58,560 --> 00:22:59,760
You're off work?

452
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:01,360
What are you doing here?

453
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:05,680
Look at that big black cloud in the sky.

454
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,920
It's going to rain soon.

455
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:10,240
Right! Let's hurry home.

456
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:12,000
Before it starts to rain, let's go...

457
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:20,520
See? Told you. Am I brilliant or what?

458
00:23:21,040 --> 00:23:23,080
Yes! Why didn't you open the umbrella?

459
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:25,760
Right!
Hurry up, brat!

460
00:23:25,840 --> 00:23:28,040
It's open...
Good!

461
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:43,120
Tai-di...

462
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:54,360
Dad, what are you doing here?

463
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:56,160
Hurry home!

464
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:59,360
If you get wet,

465
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:01,680
they'll scold me for making you sick.

466
00:24:04,320 --> 00:24:10,040
No, they won't...it's raining.

467
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:17,120
Chung B would have been here
if he was still alive.

468
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:18,800
He loved you very much.

469
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:22,720
Sis, you haven't eaten all night.

470
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:24,720
I'll tell you a joke,

471
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:28,360
if you think it's funny,
you must finish the noodles.

472
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:34,720
Rice noodles said, don't think I won't
recognize you after you ionized your hair.

473
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:35,680
Is that right?

474
00:24:38,760 --> 00:24:40,400
That's an old joke.

475
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:41,880
But you're laughing.

476
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:45,200
You laughed, you must eat.

477
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:46,640
Come on, Sis!

478
00:24:47,200 --> 00:24:48,880
Very well...It's delicious...

479
00:24:51,920 --> 00:24:56,240
Come on, let's go.

480
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:04,960
Aren't we going home, Dad?

481
00:25:09,920 --> 00:25:11,080
Dad...

482
00:25:17,160 --> 00:25:24,400
I don't like the things they said
about you...

483
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:27,680
What is it this time?

484
00:25:31,720 --> 00:25:34,560
I'm going home if you won't tell me.

485
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:36,960
OK...I'll tell you.

486
00:25:39,760 --> 00:25:45,360
They said you saw Chung B drowning

487
00:25:45,440 --> 00:25:47,640
but didn't save him.

488
00:25:47,720 --> 00:25:51,320
You wanted him dead.

489
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:10,520
You wouldn't...you loved Chung B.

490
00:26:12,800 --> 00:26:13,560
Stop!

491
00:26:17,080 --> 00:26:18,080
I'll carry that.

492
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:19,680
OK!

493
00:26:23,360 --> 00:26:24,960
Chung B, you're home!

494
00:26:25,200 --> 00:26:29,800
Dad!
Your shoulders are wet.

495
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:34,240
You wanted to cover Chung B.

496
00:26:34,600 --> 00:26:40,640
That's why I gave Chung B a big umbrella

497
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:44,960
so he could keep you dry.

498
00:26:45,560 --> 00:26:49,040
You won't get your head wet

499
00:26:49,120 --> 00:26:52,560
and be stupid like me.

500
00:26:54,040 --> 00:26:59,120
Dad...how silly of you!

501
00:27:01,920 --> 00:27:04,760
Chung too!

502
00:27:08,840 --> 00:27:13,440
Chung was really good to me.

503
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:18,160
It was my fault.

504
00:27:20,480 --> 00:27:26,160
Why do you say that?

505
00:27:31,200 --> 00:27:33,640
Don't cry...

506
00:27:37,680 --> 00:27:39,360
Well, Dad? Want another toast?

507
00:27:39,440 --> 00:27:40,160
Morning, Madam Han.

508
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:45,840
Don't eat that, it's burnt. Eat this one.

509
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:46,840
Why?

510
00:27:47,360 --> 00:27:49,200
I heard you coughing.

511
00:27:49,280 --> 00:27:51,360
The burnt toast will give you
internal heat, right?

512
00:27:52,120 --> 00:27:54,960
Since when have you become close?

513
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:58,160
Chung is gone. I want to take
better care of Dad.

514
00:27:59,120 --> 00:28:00,160
Tai-di...

515
00:28:00,240 --> 00:28:02,960
Can you put on butter for me?

516
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:05,680
Sure! You want condensed milk?

517
00:28:05,760 --> 00:28:06,840
A toast with butter and condensed milk?

518
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:07,560
Sure!

519
00:28:08,560 --> 00:28:12,400
You never know what some
people are thinking.

520
00:28:12,720 --> 00:28:14,480
The better they treat you,

521
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:16,480
the more they want to hurt you.

522
00:28:16,560 --> 00:28:18,360
Stay away from people like that.

523
00:28:18,440 --> 00:28:19,200
What?

524
00:28:19,400 --> 00:28:20,960
Time to go to the DAC.

525
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:24,760
Mom, bye, I'm going.

526
00:28:30,080 --> 00:28:31,440
Don't be upset.

527
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:34,080
I'm not.

528
00:28:34,920 --> 00:28:37,120
When I pick you up, I'll buy you candy.

529
00:28:37,240 --> 00:28:37,840
No need.

530
00:28:39,600 --> 00:28:41,680
You're so clumsy. Are you OK?

531
00:28:41,920 --> 00:28:45,600
I'm fine. It wasn't my fault.

532
00:28:45,680 --> 00:28:46,160
OK...

533
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:50,320
Trash should go in the trash can.

534
00:28:50,520 --> 00:28:54,520
Maybe people think the box is new,
leaving it out, people make take it.

535
00:28:54,720 --> 00:29:01,520
Mom said new things should be recycled.

536
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:12,280
I remember Mom threw
her favorite jacket in the trash can.

537
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:17,320
I asked her why she threw away
something so new.

538
00:29:17,440 --> 00:29:21,840
She took it back.

539
00:29:23,280 --> 00:29:24,600
When was this?

540
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:29,320
The day after Chung B died.

541
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,640
Which jacket?

542
00:29:31,920 --> 00:29:37,880
Her favorite...with woolen fringes.

543
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:41,920
You have no business in the village office.

544
00:29:42,160 --> 00:29:44,320
You don't need to come in anymore.

545
00:29:44,640 --> 00:29:47,200
Stay home and wait on Chi.

546
00:29:47,280 --> 00:29:48,520
Don't count on Chau to do it.

547
00:29:48,760 --> 00:29:50,720
You're the wife.

548
00:29:51,880 --> 00:29:52,640
Fine!

549
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:56,960
Auntie Chu!
Yes?

550
00:29:57,040 --> 00:29:59,440
Get some oranges from Wong Kee
for ancestral worship.

551
00:29:59,560 --> 00:30:01,880
The owner went back to his hometown.
It's closed.

552
00:30:02,240 --> 00:30:05,200
When you went there last week,
the owner already told you...

553
00:30:05,280 --> 00:30:06,880
Sh...shut up!

554
00:30:14,120 --> 00:30:17,440
The Police was looking for the owner
of Wong Kee.

555
00:30:17,560 --> 00:30:20,640
I told them he won't be back
for another two days.

556
00:30:20,720 --> 00:30:21,920
I wonder what they want with him.

557
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:23,880
Did the owner break the law?

558
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:27,120
I don't know. Maybe it was a routine check.

559
00:30:27,360 --> 00:30:29,760
Mother went to the fruit stand last week.

560
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:31,680
Why didn't she want Brother Nam
to mention it?

561
00:30:31,880 --> 00:30:33,440
Did she go there to buy sugarcane?

562
00:30:33,760 --> 00:30:35,520
The day after Chung died,

563
00:30:35,600 --> 00:30:37,600
why did she throw away her jacket?

564
00:30:37,760 --> 00:30:40,080
The one with woolen fringes.

565
00:30:40,320 --> 00:30:42,400
She was wearing that when
she identified the body.

566
00:30:43,040 --> 00:30:44,800
Did she go to the village house that night?

567
00:30:51,920 --> 00:30:54,520
She brought it back. Where is it?

568
00:30:55,280 --> 00:30:56,280
Brother Nam!

569
00:30:57,520 --> 00:30:58,400
Are you going back to the shop?

570
00:30:58,480 --> 00:30:59,080
Yes!

571
00:30:59,360 --> 00:31:01,120
Can I hitch a ride to Kowloon?

572
00:31:01,200 --> 00:31:01,840
Get in.

573
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:03,800
Where are you going?

574
00:31:03,880 --> 00:31:05,440
Nanking Street.

575
00:31:06,200 --> 00:31:07,600
Nanking Street...

576
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:09,800
You like driving this car?

577
00:31:10,360 --> 00:31:12,720
Kin-kwok bought a new car

578
00:31:12,960 --> 00:31:14,640
and gave it to me in less than six months.

579
00:31:14,760 --> 00:31:15,800
It's great.

580
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:18,800
Father was kind to you.

581
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:22,400
When you started a paper product shop
a couple of years ago,

582
00:31:22,560 --> 00:31:24,760
he only collected a token rent from you.

583
00:31:25,080 --> 00:31:27,680
If you need to open one of similar size

584
00:31:27,800 --> 00:31:28,960
the rent should be quite expensive.

585
00:31:29,080 --> 00:31:30,960
I have been a good help to Kin-kwok.

586
00:31:31,240 --> 00:31:33,360
And I have a tight trap.

587
00:31:34,840 --> 00:31:37,560
Nobody knew about you two
these past few years.

588
00:31:37,960 --> 00:31:40,600
One should know when to shut up

589
00:31:40,680 --> 00:31:42,880
and when to start talking.

590
00:31:44,240 --> 00:31:45,760
What do you want to know?

591
00:31:46,360 --> 00:31:47,640
The night Chung died,

592
00:31:47,840 --> 00:31:50,640
did you see Mother buying sugarcane
from Wong Kee?

593
00:31:55,960 --> 00:31:57,680
Why didn't you tell the Police?

594
00:31:57,880 --> 00:32:01,440
The Police said Chung was murdered.

595
00:32:01,720 --> 00:32:04,000
He choked on sugarcane.

596
00:32:04,200 --> 00:32:06,240
I need to know if Mother was involved.

597
00:32:06,440 --> 00:32:08,720
Cousin Han always doted on Chung.

598
00:32:09,200 --> 00:32:11,920
Even if she was angry with him,
she wouldn't kill him.

599
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:13,600
You're overthinking.

600
00:32:16,080 --> 00:32:17,120
Let me get this.

601
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:23,200
What?

602
00:32:23,320 --> 00:32:25,440
Nam, don't shoot off your mouth.

603
00:32:25,560 --> 00:32:27,200
Don't tell anyone anything about us.

604
00:32:27,320 --> 00:32:29,440
You're in trouble if anything
should happen to me.

605
00:32:29,680 --> 00:32:33,120
I know. Don't be a nag.

606
00:32:39,360 --> 00:32:41,800
Your mother-in-law is my cousin.

607
00:32:42,200 --> 00:32:44,160
But Chung is my godson.

608
00:32:44,760 --> 00:32:47,440
If anyone hurt him, I won't keep
my mouth shut.

609
00:33:04,080 --> 00:33:05,920
Honey...

610
00:33:06,920 --> 00:33:07,800
What?

611
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:10,560
Is my drawing pretty?

612
00:33:15,400 --> 00:33:17,880
I told you to stay away from Tai-di.

613
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:21,680
She hid Chung in a village house
for a reason.

614
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:24,400
Tai-di hated Chung since she was little.

615
00:33:24,520 --> 00:33:25,680
She wanted him dead.

616
00:33:26,280 --> 00:33:29,520
No...that's not what happened.

617
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:34,560
Tai-di, are you OK?

618
00:33:37,560 --> 00:33:40,480
Auntie Chau said the fever from a flu

619
00:33:40,600 --> 00:33:43,040
may cause meningitis and make me stupid.

620
00:33:43,240 --> 00:33:47,160
Then I could play with you and Chung B.

621
00:33:47,600 --> 00:33:49,520
I sat in the river for a long time,

622
00:33:49,880 --> 00:33:51,720
now I feel feverish.

623
00:33:52,760 --> 00:33:55,040
Have I become stupid now?

624
00:33:55,920 --> 00:33:58,480
Why did you do it, silly?

625
00:33:58,760 --> 00:34:02,360
Dad, when I was in the river,

626
00:34:02,560 --> 00:34:06,080
I already had a fever.

627
00:34:06,480 --> 00:34:08,360
Chung tried to pull me up,

628
00:34:08,640 --> 00:34:11,600
but I was groggy and weak.

629
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:14,000
I didn't know Chung was drowning.

630
00:34:14,240 --> 00:34:15,920
Auntie Chau got the wrong idea

631
00:34:16,120 --> 00:34:18,200
and thought I pushed hm in the water.

632
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:20,480
That's not what happened...

633
00:34:20,800 --> 00:34:23,760
I didn't...I didn't let him drown...

634
00:34:23,960 --> 00:34:28,000
Tai-di really loved Chung B...

635
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:32,400
Is it possible Tai-di was not
jealous of Chung?

636
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:35,600
Chung willingly wanted to give her $2M?

637
00:34:39,680 --> 00:34:43,280
Mok Kai-wing confirmed
it was Cheung Siu-chung's idea

638
00:34:43,440 --> 00:34:46,960
to revise the trust fund
and give $2M to Cheung Tai-di.

639
00:34:47,160 --> 00:34:49,680
He gave specific instructions
not to disclose anything.

640
00:34:49,960 --> 00:34:52,200
Cheung Tai-di knew nothing about it.

641
00:34:52,760 --> 00:34:56,080
Cheug Tai-di maybe jealous of
her brother when she was little.

642
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:58,760
But it doesn't mean they can't be close
when they grew up.

643
00:34:58,960 --> 00:35:01,240
I checked the CCTV and asked her friends.

644
00:35:01,480 --> 00:35:03,040
She was out drinking that night.

645
00:35:03,280 --> 00:35:03,920
She wasn't lying.

646
00:35:04,040 --> 00:35:07,040
Tang Suk-han and Leung Yuet-ping
don't get along.

647
00:35:07,320 --> 00:35:09,280
Leung Yuet-ping didn't particularly dote
on her son.

648
00:35:09,480 --> 00:35:12,320
The odd thing was after Cheung Kin-kwok died

649
00:35:12,560 --> 00:35:15,360
Tang Suk-han seemed to hate
Cheung Siu-chung.

650
00:35:16,360 --> 00:35:19,760
Other than the inheritance,
could there be other reasons?

651
00:35:20,480 --> 00:35:26,400
Cheung Siu-chung's smart watch,
could have told us his time of death.

652
00:35:26,600 --> 00:35:27,920
Too bad we couldn't find it.

653
00:35:29,120 --> 00:35:30,320
Hello? Yes, speaking.

654
00:35:31,200 --> 00:35:32,480
You're sure about October 15?

655
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:34,800
OK, thank you.

656
00:35:35,480 --> 00:35:38,400
The owner of the fruit store
in Ko Cho Village is back from China.

657
00:35:38,600 --> 00:35:40,320
He said the night Cheung Siu-chung died,

658
00:35:40,440 --> 00:35:41,600
Tang Suk-han bought sugarcane from him.

659
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:43,840
Sze Sir, this lady wants to see you.

660
00:35:44,200 --> 00:35:44,800
Thank you.

661
00:35:44,880 --> 00:35:47,840
Sze Sir, Cheung Sir, I wish to add
something to my statement.

662
00:35:47,920 --> 00:35:48,880
Go ahead.

663
00:35:49,120 --> 00:35:52,880
My husband told me inadvertently that
on the day after Chung died,

664
00:35:53,040 --> 00:35:54,400
my mother-in-law threw away her jacket.

665
00:35:54,640 --> 00:35:56,880
If she didn't have anything to hide,
why would she do that?

666
00:35:56,960 --> 00:35:59,040
Was the jacket related to the case?

667
00:35:59,200 --> 00:36:00,400
The night Chung died,

668
00:36:00,520 --> 00:36:03,360
my mother-in-law wore it
to identify the body.

669
00:36:03,720 --> 00:36:07,240
Are you suggesting Tang Suk-han
went to the village house that night,

670
00:36:07,320 --> 00:36:09,920
but didn't want anyone to know,
so she threw out the jacket?

671
00:36:11,320 --> 00:36:13,360
You suspect she killed her grandson?

672
00:36:13,680 --> 00:36:16,680
According to Brother Nam,
on the night Chung died,

673
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:18,960
Mother bought sugarcane from Wong Kee.

674
00:36:19,560 --> 00:36:21,760
I wanted to ask Brother Nam about it,

675
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:23,840
but I found out something else.

676
00:36:35,560 --> 00:36:36,680
(From Ko Cho Village to Wan Mei Village)

677
00:36:36,760 --> 00:36:37,920
(Oct 15, Wan Mei Village)

678
00:36:39,120 --> 00:36:40,640
I dared not ask Brother Nam directly.

679
00:36:40,720 --> 00:36:42,320
I was worried he'd destroy the evidence.

680
00:36:43,080 --> 00:36:48,000
I suspect Mother told Brother Nam
to drive her to Wan Mei Village

681
00:36:48,080 --> 00:36:48,800
to kill Chung.

682
00:36:49,200 --> 00:36:51,160
I think Mother is the prime suspect.

683
00:36:51,240 --> 00:36:53,360
It's so sad how Chung died.

684
00:36:53,600 --> 00:36:55,520
How is this Brother Nam related to you?

685
00:36:57,080 --> 00:37:00,120
Tang Heung-nam is Mother's cousin.

686
00:37:00,200 --> 00:37:01,840
He's also Chung's godfather.

687
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:05,280
He runs a coffin shop in Hunghom
and is also a Taoist priest.

688
00:37:05,680 --> 00:37:07,760
He's well connected and has clout.

689
00:37:08,120 --> 00:37:10,120
He almost has the monopoly on
all funerals in the walled villages

690
00:37:10,200 --> 00:37:11,200
in the New Territories.

691
00:37:11,360 --> 00:37:13,720
How is his relationship with Tang Suk-han?

692
00:37:14,080 --> 00:37:15,520
Mother always trusted him.

693
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:18,240
When Father left everything to Chung,

694
00:37:18,440 --> 00:37:20,000
I'm not sure if she was so angry,

695
00:37:20,400 --> 00:37:22,680
she took Brother Nam with her to kill Chung.

696
00:37:28,400 --> 00:37:31,600
Police! Can we have a word?

697
00:37:32,080 --> 00:37:32,720
Sure!

698
00:37:32,840 --> 00:37:35,040
What's your relationship with Tan Suk-han?

699
00:37:35,400 --> 00:37:37,520
She's my cousin.

700
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:40,160
Kin-kwok and I hit it off well.

701
00:37:40,440 --> 00:37:42,240
I took care of his funeral.

702
00:37:42,480 --> 00:37:46,120
Do you know Cheung Kin-kwok didn't
leave anything to his wife?

703
00:37:46,440 --> 00:37:48,480
Did they have a fight over anything?

704
00:37:48,880 --> 00:37:51,200
Maybe he felt closer to Chung.

705
00:37:51,560 --> 00:37:54,240
Then Cheung Wang-chi should be closer.

706
00:37:54,520 --> 00:37:57,240
It's hard to say how people got along.

707
00:37:58,720 --> 00:38:00,080
I'll cut to the chase.

708
00:38:00,400 --> 00:38:02,560
Where were you the night
Cheung Siu-chung died?

709
00:38:03,160 --> 00:38:04,080
I don't remember.

710
00:38:04,160 --> 00:38:08,960
No? Mind if we look at your
navigation search log?

711
00:38:09,320 --> 00:38:11,280
Check the night of October 15.

712
00:38:11,360 --> 00:38:13,680
Did he search the route to Wan Mei Village?

713
00:38:17,040 --> 00:38:20,560
It shows the route from Ko Cho Village
to Wan Mei Village.

714
00:38:20,760 --> 00:38:23,760
We found out you and Tang Suk-han
bought sugarcane

715
00:38:23,880 --> 00:38:26,000
and then went to Wan Mei Village.

716
00:38:26,120 --> 00:38:28,880
Did you two kill Cheung Siu-chung?

717
00:38:29,160 --> 00:38:30,800
Don't try to pin that on me.

718
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:32,640
Why were you there?

719
00:38:32,960 --> 00:38:36,800
I ran into Cousin Han at the fruit store.

720
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:39,280
She wanted me to drive her to
Wan Mei Village.

721
00:38:39,520 --> 00:38:41,200
I stayed in the car the whole time.

722
00:38:41,280 --> 00:38:42,560
I didn't know what happened.

723
00:38:42,760 --> 00:38:45,040
How did she know the address?

724
00:38:45,160 --> 00:38:47,840
She got it from Tai-di's phone.

725
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:50,000
What time was that?

726
00:38:50,280 --> 00:38:52,880
Around 11p.m., I really don't remember.

727
00:38:53,120 --> 00:38:56,560
What did Tang Suk-han want
with Cheung Siu-chung?

728
00:38:56,760 --> 00:38:58,400
Probably about the money.

729
00:38:58,600 --> 00:39:00,640
She didn't tell me. I didn't ask.

730
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:02,480
Then I drove her home.

731
00:39:02,760 --> 00:39:05,280
When she got back into the car,
what was her reaction?

732
00:39:05,480 --> 00:39:08,400
She looked pissed and wanted to go home.

733
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:12,480
How would you describe her relationship
with Cheung Siu-chung?

734
00:39:13,160 --> 00:39:15,040
She always doted on Chung.

735
00:39:15,120 --> 00:39:18,400
But after she found out Kin-kwok
and her daughter-in-law had an affair...

736
00:39:19,880 --> 00:39:22,400
Cheung Kin-kwok and Leung Yuet-ping?

737
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:24,320
I shouldn't have said that.

738
00:39:24,440 --> 00:39:27,240
After that, she was angry with Chung.

739
00:39:27,440 --> 00:39:29,160
Who else knows about this?

740
00:39:29,240 --> 00:39:31,360
Everyone in the house.

741
00:39:31,440 --> 00:39:34,760
But nobody in the village.

742
00:39:35,600 --> 00:39:38,680
After Kin-kwok left everything to Chung,

743
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:43,520
Cousin Han suspected Chung's father
was someone else

744
00:39:43,640 --> 00:39:44,880
and they were after the money.

745
00:39:45,680 --> 00:39:50,680
The crazy thing was
Cousin Han thought it was me.

746
00:39:51,120 --> 00:39:52,680
That was so unfair!

747
00:39:52,920 --> 00:39:55,600
But in the end, Ping admitted it.

748
00:39:55,800 --> 00:39:58,800
Chung was Kin-kwok's son.

749
00:39:59,160 --> 00:40:02,960
Cousin Han was furious.

750
00:40:03,160 --> 00:40:06,200
Cheung Siu-chung was Cheung Kin-kwok
and Leung Yuet-ping's son?!

751
00:40:06,520 --> 00:40:12,160
That's why Kin-kwok left Chung everything.

752
00:40:12,760 --> 00:40:16,320
It was better than giving it to Chi.

753
00:40:16,560 --> 00:40:19,440
If you knew about this,
why didn't you tell the Police?

754
00:40:19,760 --> 00:40:23,360
I only found out later Chung died
inside the village house.

755
00:40:23,600 --> 00:40:25,720
I didn't want any trouble.

756
00:40:26,080 --> 00:40:28,120
Cousin Han told me to keep my mouth shut.

757
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:31,120
I didn't want any trouble.

758
00:40:33,880 --> 00:40:35,280
This way, officers!

759
00:40:41,960 --> 00:40:42,720
Grandma!

760
00:40:44,200 --> 00:40:46,800
Ms. Tang Suk-han, this is a search warrant.

761
00:40:47,160 --> 00:40:48,480
We have reasons to believe

762
00:40:48,600 --> 00:40:51,600
you're hiding crucial evidence in
the murder of Cheung Siu-chung.

763
00:40:51,800 --> 00:40:53,120
We need to search your room.

764
00:40:53,240 --> 00:40:56,400
What crime have I committed?
Why do you want to search my room?

765
00:40:56,520 --> 00:40:58,160
The Police have a search warrant
issued by the court.

766
00:40:58,240 --> 00:40:59,640
They have the right to search the house.

767
00:40:59,880 --> 00:41:00,480
Thank you.

768
00:41:02,320 --> 00:41:04,200
Don't mess up my things.

769
00:41:19,040 --> 00:41:20,960
What is it doing here?

770
00:41:21,120 --> 00:41:22,720
Is this your jacket?

771
00:41:22,960 --> 00:41:25,920
Yes...no! I threw it away.

772
00:41:27,880 --> 00:41:30,960
I took it to the cleaner...

773
00:41:31,360 --> 00:41:33,760
I don't remember.

774
00:41:34,200 --> 00:41:37,040
Sze Sir, we found Cheung Siu-chung's watch.

775
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:37,920
What?

776
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:41,440
That's Chung's watch!

777
00:41:41,800 --> 00:41:43,640
Why do you have it?

778
00:41:43,720 --> 00:41:45,160
I thought the watch was lost.

779
00:41:45,240 --> 00:41:47,520
Grandma, why didn't you tell us you had it?

780
00:41:55,640 --> 00:41:58,560
You went to Wan Mei Village that night?
You wanted Chung to split the money.

781
00:41:58,960 --> 00:42:01,840
He refused and you killed him in a rage!

782
00:42:02,080 --> 00:42:04,640
After you found out the watch stopped
after midnight,

783
00:42:04,720 --> 00:42:06,080
you were afraid you won't get
the inheritance,

784
00:42:06,160 --> 00:42:07,840
that's why you hid the watch, am I right?

785
00:42:07,920 --> 00:42:09,400
Don't go shooting off your mouth!

786
00:42:09,480 --> 00:42:12,600
I don't know why the watch is in here.

787
00:42:12,800 --> 00:42:18,800
Mom...I saw you throw away the watch.

788
00:42:18,880 --> 00:42:23,760
I picked it up and put it back
in the drawer.

789
00:42:24,840 --> 00:42:26,120
Ms. Tang Suk-han,

790
00:42:26,200 --> 00:42:29,160
we suspect you're connected to a murder
in Wan Mei Village.

791
00:42:29,240 --> 00:42:30,480
You're now under arrest.
